ps://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/issues/4454#issuecomment-35402709","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mrdoob/three.js/issues/4454","id":35402709,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM1NDAyNzA5","user":{"login":"ghost","id":10137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost","html_url":"https://github.com/ghost","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2014-02-18T16:31:49Z","updated_at":"2014-02-18T16:31:49Z","body":"Agreed. Case testing would be nice too but ain't nobody got time for that. :p\n\n-----Original Message-----\nFrom: \"Tarek Sherif\" notifications@github.com\nSent: ‎18/‎02/‎2014 7:37 PM\nTo: \"mrdoob/three.js\" three.js@noreply.github.com\nSubject: Re: [three.js] Physically-based shading became an unchangeabledefault? (#4454)\n\nOne final thought: I think it might have been a good idea to gradually roll out this change out over a couple of revisions. Maybe make physicallyBasedShading default to true for one revision (possibly with deprecation warnings if they set it to false), and then if there are no problems for that revision, make it the only choice. Probably any changes to the shaders produced should be done in this way? That way you can test them out on everyone's hardware before making the change final.\n—\nRep